  "description": "Follows the Ugaritic storm god Baal through his rivalry with Sea, the negotiations and craftsmanship that secure his palace, and his disappearance and return in the struggle with Death. Explores divine kingship, Anat’s actions, the relation of rain and fertility to political order, comparative ancient Near Eastern poetry, and the limits of reconstructing the story from six damaged tablets.",
